the ctor stays ACC_PUBLIC in bytecode so the companion's `apply`/`copy` keep
calling it; an already-compiled caller keeps linking (on Scala 2). The report
guards recompilation: source built against the new version can no longer call
`new A`. On Scala 3 the app does fail, but for the unrelated, already-tracked
reason that `apply`/`copy` themselves go bytecode-private there.
